# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/

# The LVGL Pro CLI compiles an emscripten preview runtime into the project the
# first time a screenshot is taken. Both are caches; deleting them costs a slow
# rebuild and nothing else.
preview-build/
#preview-bin/

# ── Generated by `lvglpro generate .` ───────────────────────────────────────
# The XML is the source. Everything below is derived from it and from the assets
# in images/ and fonts/, and a checkout is not buildable until it is regenerated:
#
#     lvglpro generate .
#
# It is out of the repo because it is large, entirely mechanical, and produces a
# diff on every run - reviewing a change to a screen would otherwise mean reading
# the same change twice, once in the XML and once in the C it emits.
#*_gen.c
#*_gen.h
#*_gen.cmake

# Converted assets. The sources are tracked - images/*.png and the font .ttf
# faces - and these are the same bytes re-emitted as C arrays by the resource
# converter. A font blob is rewritten in full whenever a size or glyph range
# changes, and a single background image can run to megabytes.
#images/*_data.c
#fonts/*_data.c

# ── Editor / tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-machine config and caches, not project source.
.claude/
.vscode/
.mcp.json
.cache/
.cache.json

# ── OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
